# Browser
# Summon: Brynhildr's chapter I (turn 1) exiles Bot1's Lightning Bolt, which says over its art that it is playable "during any
# turn you put a lore counter on Summon: Brynhildr". Turn 2 is Bot2's: Bot2's Tezzeret's Gambit proliferates the Saga's lore
# counter, so a lore counter goes on it this turn, but not by Bot1 ("you put"), and the Bolt can't be cast; nor once Bot1
# itself puts a +1/+1 counter on the Saga (Take Up the Shield) - not a lore counter - though its Mox Ruby is untapped. Turn 3: Bot1 puts the third lore counter
# on it, chapter III resolves and the Saga is sacrificed (CR 714.4), and the Bolt is cast from exile anyway: it is this
# turn's counter that counts, whatever became of the Saga since.

